# Plan - tb-metrics-remainder

**Feature:** `tb-metrics-remainder`
**Spec:** [`spec.md`](spec.md)
**Design:** [`design.md`](design.md)
**Interview:** [`interview.md`](interview.md)
**Created:** 2026-11-27

## Inputs

- `spec.md` controls scope, required behavior and rubric mapping.
- `design.md` supplies the chosen shape and constraints.
- `interview.md` supplies the settled decisions D1-D11.

## Strategy

One slice and one PR into `main`. Edit only the reporting side:
`plugin-src/shared/resources/performance/` (`workflow-projection.js`,
`fleet.js`, a new `convergence.js`, `service.js`, `mcp.js`), the CLI command
(`cli/src/commands/metrics.js`, `cli/src/performance.js`), the desktop IPC and
metrics card, and the docs. Protocol files owned by the parallel work are read
through their exports (`scheduledBlocking`, `severityOf`, `outcomeStatus`),
not edited. Tests go in a new `cli/test/convergence-metrics.test.js`, with
small additions to existing CLI and desktop suites.

## Steps

- **P1. Schema.** Extend the observation schema in `fleet.js` with the new
  fields and their validators (AC4).
- **P2. Projection.** In `workflow-projection.js` add the finding, result,
  round, pair, reviewer, adjudication and waiver fields (AC1-AC3), and the
  projection version with reprojection (AC5).
- **P3. Measures.** New `performance/convergence.js`: a pure
  `convergence(rows)` for the four measures and the reviewer table
  (AC6-AC11), plus a Markdown renderer.
- **P4. Surfaces.** `metricsRequest('convergence')` over local latest rows or
  a dataset; CLI `metrics convergence` and the `metrics status` summary;
  reevaluation `measurement.convergence` and HTML; MCP tool (AC12). Desktop
  IPC action and card control (AC13) are a separate issue (I-5) so the
  mandated fallback never holds the docs.
- **P5. Docs and mirror.** USER-GUIDE.md, PERFORMANCE.md, PROTOCOL.md,
  cli/README.md (AC14); restage resources to the desktop mirror and run the
  plugin/resource checks.
- **P6. Verification.** Focused suites locally (with the documented Mac
  workarounds), paired review rounds on local commits, then push once and
  record hosted CI.
